# text_id = 1596
# text = From the passing of the Empire Settlement Act in 1922 until 1931 ( by which time migration , owing to the world economic depression , had temporarily ceased ) about 400,000 United Kingdom citizens emigrated to other parts of the Commonwealth , receiving assistance under the Acts at a total cost of about £ 6,000,000 , or £ 15 per head .
