# text_id = 1630
# text = As I say , the Ministers of State drawing salaries of £ 3,000 a year have , under the Ministerial Salaries Act , 1946 , been entitled always to draw £ 500 a year as Parliamentary salary and , if they could satisfy the Inland Revenue authorities , have been able to claim the whole of that as Parliamentary expenses .
