# text_id = 1693
# text = I understand that there have been experiments with Montmorillonite clay , which , when heated with radioactive material to about 1,000 degrees Centigrade , results in the production of a hard , rocky sort of substance , which absorbs almost all the radioactivity and causes it to be perfectly safe , whether exposed to ordinary fresh water or to sea water .
