# text_id = 1779
# text = I would ask whether the industry itself was as alive to its own dangers as I should have thought it would have been when , in the autumn of 1950 , 447 firms were asked to tender for drill of various types , yet only 40 offers were received , not all of which were acceptable , and which covered only 40 per cent . of the quantity needed .
