# text_id = 1787
# text = A very large population is crowded into small islands whose natural resources , never as great as is imagined , have been much reduced by former unwise methods of cultivation , and where there is , as yet , no industrial development of sufficient importance to take up the surplus population that cannot find a living in agriculture — a population which , moreover , is increasing by leaps and bounds .
