# text_id = 1824
# text = It was significant that the Attorney - General , when replying to my hon . Friend the Member for Nelson and Colne , did not reply on the merits of the issue but rather expressed sympathy and took refuge in the argument that what had been found good in Scots law about the acceptance of diminished responsibility ought , by virtue of that simple fact , to operate in England .
