# text_id = 1844
# text = We have had many thoughtful contributions to this Debate , but nothing that has been said today has for me crystallised the situation or summarised our fears so well as a single remark made in London last week by M. Paul Reynaud , when he said that if war was to break our now , the Russians would be at Calais before a single British or American Division could land there .
