# text = The Amendment is designed to ensure that the local authority shall not be called upon to make up a stretch of road — and under the Bill they can be called upon to make up anything not less than one hundred yards in length — unless that stretch which they are asked to make into a road actually touches an existing highway which is maintainable by the local ratepayers .
