# text_id = 1888
# text = I think that to say , as a generality , that production cannot lead to inflation may induce the view that all we have to do is to start producing goods , whether there is a real demand for them or not , or whether it is possible to make an economic profit out of them or not , which would be about the most inflationary thing that we could do .
