# text_id = 1925
# text = In 1953 , when those two reliefs were improved by £ 10 each , the relief for a daughter maintained by an infirm taxpayer was increased from £ 25 to £ 40 , though it must be admitted that that did not come about until my hon . and learned Friend the Member for Liverpool , Edge Hill ( Mr. A. J. Irvine ) moved an Amendment to that effect .
