# text_id = 1941
# text = Since the war , with the nationalisation of the basic industries , it has been quite rightly accepted that the Minister must play a part in those industries ; and not only does the Minister appoint the members of the boards , but in every case there was given to him the reserve power to give directives to those boards if it was considered necessary in the national interest .
