# text_id = 1944
# text = Mr. J. T. Price asked the Secretary of State for the Home Department if he is aware of the concern felt by many people interested in the preservation of our native song birds at the effect of the Protection of Birds Act , 1954 , which does not safeguard the nests of robins , skylarks and song thrushes against spoliation ; and if he will take action to remedy this situation .
