# text_id = 1951
# text = It provides that the British Service authorities may , for our convenience , exercise Customs control at our chief crossing points on the Federal frontiers over members of the forces , their dependants , civilian employees and their dependants , and employees of such organisations as the N.A.A.F.I. , and , in return , that they should ensure observance of German Customs regulations as amended by the terms of the Conventions .
