# text_id = 1964
# text = The Minister argues that it is impracticable to secure this , but the Road - Rail Agreement , 1946 , which was arrived at by practical men who really understood the industry , contained provisions which , as my hon . Friend the Member for Cardiff , South - East ( Mr. Callaghan ) pointed out , gave the users some right to protection against unfair competition between the two .
